    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0305" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856d.00/3–349</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Baruch</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-03">March 3, 1949.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 8.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 86</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram 208 of March
                    2, 1949,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d207-f1"/> I have the honor to enclose copies of
                    the letter from the Minister of Foreign Affairs transmitting documentation on
                    the consequences of a restoration of Republican authority in Djokjakarta and its
                    vicinity, together with various exhibits concerning the alleged subversive
                    activities of the Republican Government.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d207-f2"/> The
                    enclosures to Mr. Stikker’s letter <pb facs="0306" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/> are
                    sent in only one copy as the Embassy has not sufficient staff to copy these
                    lengthy papers.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Coe</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of Embassy</hi>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d207-a1.xml" xpointer="d207-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d207-a2.xml" xpointer="d207-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
